From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastien Lalancette <seblalancette@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 08:47:03 -0700
Subject: net: Rebuild proxy HttpAuthController when the proxy changes

HttpNetworkTransaction::DoGenerateProxyAuthToken() lazily creates an
HttpAuthController bound to the current proxy and previously only
created it when the pointer was null. When a transaction repeats stream
creation (such as after a keep-alive I/O error or an auth restart) and
resolves to a different proxy via fallback, the stale controller was
reused, applying the previous proxy's credentials to the new proxy.

Add HttpAuthController::MatchesSchemeHostPort() and recreate the proxy
HttpAuthController in DoGenerateProxyAuthToken() when it no longer
matches the current proxy's SchemeHostPort. Also add and update unit
tests to verify that credentials are not leaked across proxies and that
fallback proxies use their own cached credentials when available.

Fixed: 533426590
Change-Id: I8a433f4f200c8f6d954a5f081c03da60d207fa35
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8358595
Reviewed-by: mmenke <mmenke@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Sebastien Lalancette <seblalancette@chromium.org>
